  "final_text": "Generated `eta_costheta_scan_W1.7_Q2_1.5.dat` \u2014 a 5-point EXCLURAD input for the \u03b7 configuration at W=1.7 GeV, Q\u00b2=1.5 GeV\u00b2 (both well within the physical/interpolation range), \u03c6*=90\u00b0.\n\nOne correction was applied: the requested cos \u03b8* endpoints of exactly \u00b11 correspond to collinear kinematics where \u03c6* becomes undefined and the code is known to be numerically unstable there (the repo's own examples cap the range at \u00b10.999, and the README recommends a special \"skip unphysical\" runner near large |cos \u03b8*|). I kept the 5 evenly-spaced points but pulled the endpoints in to \u22120.999/+0.999 (\u22120.9990, \u22120.4995, 0.0000, 0.4995, 0.9990) to avoid that singular boundary while still spanning the full requested range. Details are in `outcome.json`."
